# Optional. A pre-funded Tron *Nile testnet* private key (64 hex chars, no 0x).
#
# Leave this unset and every visitor's browser generates its own wallet in
# localStorage, which starts empty — they must fund it at the Nile faucet
# before they can sign anything.
#
# Set it and the whole site shares one already-funded wallet, so a visitor can
# send immediately with no setup. This is the right choice for a live demo.
#
# ⚠ Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the client bundle, so this key is
# PUBLIC to anyone who opens the site and can be drained at any time. Only ever
# use a throwaway Nile testnet key holding worthless test tokens. `assertTestnet`
# in src/wallet/tronNetwork.ts refuses to run against mainnet hosts for this
# exact reason — never point this at a key with real funds.
#
# To reuse the wallet you already funded locally, run this in the browser
# console on your local dev site and copy the result:
#   JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('custos.demo.wallet.nile.v1')).privateKey
VITE_TRON_DEMO_PRIVATE_KEY=
